  "limits": [
    "Three designs \u00d7 three adapter LRs \u00d7 two fresh seeds \u00d7 full30k; no automatic selection, longer confirmation or grid expansion.",
    "Every training/model/helper source is byte-identical to the completed channel-factor runner; only study orchestration and tests are added.",
    "Channel s64 was chosen using the previous screen, so new training seeds are independent but architecture choice and reused holdout/noise are not.",
    "Produced rank8, normalized value input, parallel MLP delta, static factor offsets and common AdaLN remain unchanged.",
    "Base/null initialization and data/noise/dropout streams are paired; each design starts identically across all rates; dense/CP factor Jacobians are not matched to channel factors.",
    "Global LR8e-4 and gain1/sqrt(8) fixed; adapter multipliers1/2/4 cover every adapter parameter, including heads, scales and offsets.",
    "Equal three-point search budgets do not imply parameter/FLOP matching or establish an optimal learning rate.",
    "Prior poor finite high-rate endpoints are not discarded. All fresh endpoints are reported, including severe degradation; preflight success does not establish long-run stability.",
    "Primary comparisons use final30k CFG2 EMA FID; retain CFG1, class agreement, both seeds, all adjacent-rate effects and convergence. No best-intermediate selection.",
    "Same-rate design gaps and the prespecified channel4-minus-dense1/CP1 gaps are reported separately; the latter compare different operating rates.",
    "No static-control or channel-s32 replication in this focused LR study; conditioning benefit versus static remains prior-screen evidence.",
    "Concurrent throughput/allocation are descriptive; dedicated speed benchmarks and per-token execution remain deferred.",
    "No normalization/gain/muP change, generic checkpoints, model weights, official test, evaluator downloads, implicit resume, shared/nonlinear projector, retrieval or LM launch."
  ]
